I'm going to go ahead and add a new hospital at some random location.

3814
05:56:13,454 --> 05:56:20,164
So I basically get all of the available spaces and I randomly choose one of them as where I would like to add this particular hospital.

3815
05:56:20,878 --> 05:56:24,612
I have some logging output and generating some images, which we'll take a look at a little bit later.

3816
05:56:25,104 --> 05:56:26,692
But here is the key idea.

3817
05:56:27,264 --> 05:56:30,144
So I'm going to just keep repeating this algorithm.

3818
05:56:30,304 --> 05:56:36,420
I could specify a maximum of how many times I want it to run, or I could just run it up until it hits a local maximum or local minimum.

3819
05:56:37,166 --> 05:56:41,264
And now we'll basically consider all of the hospitals that could potentially move.

3820
05:56:41,424 --> 05:56:44,804
So consider each of the two hospitals or more hospitals if there are more than that.

3821
05:56:45,422 --> 05:56:52,228
And consider all of the places where that hospital could move to, some neighbor of that hospital that we can move the neighbor to.

3822
05:56:52,942 --> 05:56:53,808
And then see,

3823
05:56:54,848 --> 05:56:58,020
is this going to be better than where we were currently?

3824
05:56:58,414 --> 05:57:04,996
So if it is going to be better, then we'll go ahead and update our best neighbor and keep track of this new best neighbor that we found.

3825
05:57:05,774 --> 05:57:13,508
And then afterwards, we can ask ourselves the question: if best neighbor cost is greater than or equal to the cost of the current set of hospitals, meaning

3826
05:57:13,806 --> 05:57:20,868
if the cost of our best neighbor is greater than the current cost, meaning our best neighbor is worse than our current state.

3827
05:57:21,326 --> 05:57:26,852
well, then we shouldn't make any changes at all, and we should just go ahead and return the current set of hospitals.

3828
05:57:27,214 --> 05:57:32,292
But otherwise, we can update our hospitals in order to change them to one of the best neighbors.

3829
05:57:32,462 --> 05:57:37,668
And if there are multiple that are all equivalent, I'm here using random.choice to say go ahead and choose one randomly.

3830
05:57:38,318 --> 05:57:46,340
So this is really just a Python implementation of that same idea that we were just talking about: this idea of taking a current state, some current set of hospitals,

3831
05:57:46,688 --> 05:57:54,048
generating all of the neighbors, looking at all of the ways we could take one hospital and move it one square to the left or right or up or down, and then figuring out,

3832
05:57:54,128 --> 05:57:59,076
based on all of that information, which is the best neighbor or the set of all the best neighbors.

3833
05:57:59,310 --> 05:58:01,124
and then choosing from one of those.

3834
05:58:01,966 --> 05:58:04,932
And each time we go ahead and generate an image in order to do that.

3835
05:58:05,774 --> 05:58:15,396
And so now what we're doing is if we look down at the bottom, I'm going to randomly generate a space with height 10 and width 20, and I'll say, go ahead and put three hospitals somewhere in the space.

3836
