4494
06:59:43,694 --> 06:59:46,660
And here then is what the backtracking function might look like.

4495
06:59:47,566 --> 06:59:47,908
First,

4496
06:59:49,230 --> 06:59:55,492
if the assignment is complete, if I've made an assignment of every variable to a value, go ahead and just return that assignment.

4497
06:59:56,686 --> 06:59:59,428
Then we'll select an unassigned variable from that assignment.

4498
07:00:00,174 --> 07:00:08,256
Then for each of the possible values in the domain, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, let's go ahead and create a new assignment that assigns the variable to that

4499
07:00:08,256 --> 07:00:14,148
value. I'll call this consistent function, which I'll show you in a moment, that just checks to make sure this new assignment is consistent.

4500
07:00:14,638 --> 07:00:19,716
But if it is consistent, we'll go ahead and call backtrack to go ahead and continue trying to run backtracking search.

4501
07:00:20,336 --> 07:00:26,308
and as long as the result is not none, meaning it wasn't a failure, we can go ahead and return that result.

4502
07:00:26,926 --> 07:00:29,284
But if we make it through all the values and nothing works,

4503
07:00:30,254 --> 07:00:32,096
then it is a failure, there's no solution.

4504
07:00:32,398 --> 07:00:34,084
We go ahead and return none here.

4505
07:00:35,182 --> 07:00:36,096
What do these functions do?

4506
07:00:36,462 --> 07:00:39,908
Select unassigned variable is just going to choose a variable not yet assigned.

4507
07:00:40,336 --> 07:00:45,380
so it's going to loop over all the variables, and if it's not already assigned, we'll go ahead and just return that variable.

4508
07:00:46,318 --> 07:00:48,096
And what does the consistent function do?

4509
07:00:48,398 --> 07:00:51,076
Well, the consistent function goes through all the constraints.

4510
07:00:51,856 --> 07:01:02,468
and if we have a situation where we've assigned both of those values to variables, but they are the same, well then that is a violation of the constraint, in which case we'll return false.

4511
07:01:03,056 --> 07:01:07,460
but if nothing is inconsistent, then the assignment is consistent and will return true.

4512
07:01:08,718 --> 07:01:16,260
And then all the program does is it calls backtrack on an empty assignment, an empty dictionary that has no variable assigned and no values yet,

4513
07:01:16,896 --> 07:01:20,388
save that inside a solution, and then print out that solution.

4514
07:01:21,166 --> 07:01:23,364
So by running this now, I can run Python

4515
